--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scope

This licence covers the source code (app/, tools/, packaging/) and the
project's own original written, drawn and procedural content:

- the lessons, clinical correlations and radiology case texts
  (data/content/lessons*.json, clinical*.json, radiology*.json);
- the hand-written descriptions (data/content/descriptions_extra*.json);
- the model summaries (data/content/model_summaries.json) and the part guides
  of the library models (data/content/model_parts/);
- the lesson diagrams, 102 SVG files drawn for this project
  (data/content/diagrams/);
- the 38 models of the model library (data/local_model_library) that have a
  builder in this project (the procedural builders in app/micro, cached in
  data/micro_cache, and the three models built in Blender, notes in models/);
- the adapter data of the model library, 85 json files in
  app/variants/anatomy_runtime_adapters and app/variants/anatomy_variants;
- the interface icons and palettes in app/ui/resources/studio, and the
  application icon.

THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md records where this material came from, including what
the owner stated about its origin.

It does NOT cover third-party material shipped alongside, which keeps its own
licence:

- the anatomy dataset in data/anatomy and data/findings (CC BY-SA 4.0, see
  data/anatomy/LICENSE), including the definition texts in
  data/anatomy/definitions.json, about two thirds of which are Wikipedia
  excerpts (CC BY-SA 3.0). This share-alike material is still part of the app;
- the histology and radiology images (each under the licence recorded beside
  it: CC0, public domain, CC BY, or free use);
- the three library models neuron, capillary_bed and lymph_drainage in
  data/local_model_library, which this project does not claim as its own
  builds (see THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md);
- the bundled libraries and fonts.

See THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for the full list.

Anatomy Explorer is a study aid. It is not a medical device and must not be used
for diagnosis or treatment.
